{"author":{"id":"86dc3c885e4fa466d19699d4a5e74c240f1c9d6b23f4e62ea2d2d8e359bd1711"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788929796,"nonce":"mbT/6bPRp81PYDM5XChtVwOIrmM=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOUKdEis8AAAABQZOMVw","github-url":"https://github.com/ff6347/giclang/issues/8","origin":"github"},"title":"Show context lines in diagnostics","message":"When an error points at an empty or cryptic line (e.g. EOF after a trailing newline for a missing closing brace), the caret alone gives the student no context.\n\nEnhancement: render the line(s) before the error line in the diagnostic output.\n\nImplementation notes (from 2026-08 session):\n- Formatter-only change: report() already receives the full source.\n- Previous line bounds: end is lineStart - 1, start is source.lastIndexOf(\"\\\\n\", lineStart - 2) + 1.\n- Edge cases: error on line 1 (no previous line), blank previous line (print anyway).\n- Requires amending the spec's error examples first (they currently show exactly one source line).\n- Relates to the richer option of secondary spans for unclosed delimiters (point at the opening brace) — tracked in docs/milestones/diagnostic-enhancements.md.","files":null}]}